# SABOTAGE: MG-09 (ADR-049 mutation ledger) — `Samen.Pii.WriteGuard.plaintext_write?/2`
# is WIDENED so a raw `vt_*` VAULT TOKEN counts as operator-authored PLAINTEXT. A token is
# the opposite of plaintext: it is the opaque FK the domain column is allowed to hold, the
# one value `Samen.Type.VaultField.dump_to_native/2` accepts without a vault write. Writing
# it back re-states what is already stored and encrypts nothing.
#
# The OVER-refusal direction: every shipped RP-L1 test writes genuine plaintext and stays
# green under this flip. What breaks is the token round-trip an operator-plane write
# performs whenever the vaulted column's current value is carried through unchanged.
#
# Flips the named MG-09 red. The anti-tautology CONTROL stays green — genuine operator
# plaintext is still refused with "no-operator-plaintext-write" — so the red fails because
# the `vt_*` arm was widened, not because the guard or the vault write path broke. MG-08's
# and MG-10's reds stay green: this patch touches ONE clause.
#
# One case clause, one literal. Touches write_guard.ex ALONE.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/hardening/pii_write_guard_fail_closed_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: MG-09: an OPERATOR writing back the raw vt_* token is ALLOWED
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/pii/write_guard.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/pii/write_guard.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/pii/write_guard.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/pii/write_guard.ex
@@ -117,7 +117,7 @@ defmodule Samen.Pii.WriteGuard do
   defp plaintext_write?(changeset, name) do
     case Ash.Changeset.fetch_change(changeset, name) do
       {:ok, %Masked{}} -> false
-      {:ok, "vt_" <> _} -> false
+      {:ok, "vt_" <> _} -> true
       {:ok, nil} -> false
       {:ok, _plaintext} -> true
       :error -> false
